(C)  ADAPTIVE BAND ADDS INFORMATION OVER THE FIXED BAND
     published: beta = +0.0020, LRT chi2 = 11.6, p = 6.6e-04
==============================================================================================

  LMM added-term LRT (published)              beta = +0.00202, chi2(1) = 11.61, p = 6.56e-04
  logit GEE, trial clusters                   beta = +0.00410, p = 0.6820
  logit GEE, subject clusters                 beta = +0.00002, p = 0.9989
  cloglog person-period, subject clusters     beta = -0.00232, p = 0.8546
  logit person-period, subject clusters       beta = -0.00214, p = 0.8723

  Each signal on its own -- does it predict failure at all?
    signal                  published LMM (crash5)       person-period cloglog
    above                      b=+0.0511 p=7.6e-10           b=+0.527 p=0.0138
    excess_fixed               b=+0.0013 p=1.0e-08           b=+0.027 p=0.0000
    excess_adaptive            b=+0.0016 p=3.4e-11           b=+0.019 p=0.0046

    The two graded signals correlate at r = 0.914. Each predicts
    failure on its own. What does not survive is the claim that the
    ADAPTIVE reference adds information over the fixed one: entered
    together, the fixed excess keeps the effect and the adaptive one
    contributes nothing. The published ordering reverses.

